    expectedAnswer: "Use a heap when you repeatedly need the minimum/maximum item, top-K values, dynamic scheduling, or a priority queue. Heap insertion and removal are O(log n); peeking is O(1).",
    deepExplanation: "Step 1 — Identify the pattern signal.\n\nStep 1 — Min-heap implementation.\n\nWITHOUT BUILT-IN / CORE:\n```ts\nclass MinHeap {\n  private readonly heap: number[] = [];\n\n  get size(): number {\n    return this.heap.length;\n  }\n\n  peek(): number | undefined {\n    return this.heap[0];\n  }\n\n  push(value: number): void {\n    this.heap.push(value);\n    let i = this.heap.length - 1;\n\n    while (i > 0) {\n      const parent = Math.floor((i - 1) / 2);\n      if (this.heap[parent]! <= this.heap[i]!) break;\n\n      [this.heap[parent], this.heap[i]] = [this.heap[i]!, this.heap[parent]!];\n      i = parent;\n    }\n  }\n\n  pop(): number | undefined {\n    if (this.heap.length === 0) return undefined;\n    if (this.heap.length === 1) return this.heap.pop();\n\n    const root = this.heap[0]!;\n    this.heap[0] = this.heap.pop()!;\n\n    let i = 0;\n\n    while (true) {\n      const left = i * 2 + 1;\n      const right = i * 2 + 2;\n      let smallest = i;\n\n      if (left < this.heap.length && this.heap[left]! < this.heap[smallest]!) {\n        smallest = left;\n      }\n\n      if (right < this.heap.length && this.heap[right]! < this.heap[smallest]!) {\n        smallest = right;\n      }\n\n      if (smallest === i) break;\n\n      [this.heap[i], this.heap[smallest]] =\n        [this.heap[smallest]!, this.heap[i]!];\n      i = smallest;\n    }\n\n    return root;\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWITH BUILT-IN baseline:\n```ts\nfunction priorityQueueUsingSort(values: readonly number[]): number[] {\n  return [...values].sort((a, b) => a - b);\n}\n```\n\nExample:\npush 5,2,4\npop → 2\npeek → 4.\n\nComplexity:\nHeap push/pop O(log n), peek O(1).\nRepeated sorting is typically O(n log n) and is not equivalent to a dynamic heap.\n\nStep 5 — Interview takeaway:\nUse the pattern only when its invariant and assumptions actually hold.",
